{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/OpenGL Drawing in Blender.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/OpenGL Drawing in Blender.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"open gl drawing in blender open gl drawing in blender","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/OpenGL Drawing in Blender.md","fileName":"OpenGL Drawing in Blender.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"OpenGL Drawing in Blender","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 09:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Viewport Drawing API]] · [[Blender Editor Construction]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Viewport Drawing API","Blender Editor Construction","Blender Immediate-Mode GPU Drawing","Blender Region Draw Dispatch","blenderpythonapi.pdf","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/OpenGL Drawing in Blender.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/OpenGL Drawing in Blender.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"open gl drawing in blender open gl drawing in blender","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/OpenGL Drawing in Blender.md","fileName":"OpenGL Drawing in Blender.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"OpenGL Drawing in Blender","heading":"OpenGL Drawing in Blender","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"OpenGL-style drawing in Blender can place transient lines and shapes over a 3D Viewport without adding mesh objects to the scene. A draw callback enables the required graphics state, issues line or vertex commands in canvas coordinates, and then disables or resets that state.\n\nRestoring defaults after every draw helps the overlay cooperate with Blender and other add-ons that share the graphics context. Because the source targets Blender 2.78c and OpenGL 2.1-style `bgl`, exact functions are version-specific, but disciplined state management remains a general requirement for shared viewport drawing.\n\nCore editor code can avoid direct OpenGL calls by using Blender's GPU abstraction. The tutorial editor clears a region and emits colored rectangles through [[Blender Immediate-Mode GPU Drawing]], allowing the [[Blender Region Draw Dispatch]] path to render through application-owned shaders, buffers, and state.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Viewport Drawing API","Blender Editor Construction","Blender Immediate-Mode GPU Drawing","Blender Region Draw Dispatch","blenderpythonapi.pdf","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/OpenGL Drawing in Blender.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/OpenGL Drawing in Blender.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"open gl drawing in blender open gl drawing in blender","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/OpenGL Drawing in Blender.md","fileName":"OpenGL Drawing in Blender.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"OpenGL Drawing in Blender","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[blenderpythonapi.pdf]]\n\n[[coreblenderdevelopment.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Viewport Drawing API","Blender Editor Construction","Blender Immediate-Mode GPU Drawing","Blender Region Draw Dispatch","blenderpythonapi.pdf","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}